      },
      "lineNbr": 664,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T12:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fact that we have \"name\" and \"test\" is a bit confusing to me. Why not use \"benchmark\" instead of name?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 664,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 664,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "47af5aed5a7a3a6b305820d692b79f0336dc0d60",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "507fbe97_6126c48f",
        "filename": "bench/BazelBenchmarkRunner.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 664,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T19:45:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Dropping \"test\" (rationale in the below comment).\n\nI think \"benchmark\" is a bit ambiguous because we have benchmark names and benchmark types. Also, setting \"name\" to the return value of `getName()` seems more natural to me than setting \"benchmark\" to `getName()`.",
      "parentUuid": "8e818918_83fe7549",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 664,
        "startChar": 22,
        "endLine": 664,
        "endChar": 26
      },
      "revId": "47af5aed5a7a3a6b305820d692b79f0336dc0d60",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "34f04a54_e5705325",
        "filename": "bench/BazelBenchmarkRunner.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 670,
      "author": {
        "id": 5395
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T12:52:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027m not sure the value of the uniqueName() in the benchmark - it defaults to just the name for everything except SKPAnimationBench and SKPBench. IMO, we get rid of it so there\u0027s just one name.\n\nWith that out of the way, should we just put width and height as their own keys? or a combined key \"dimensions\"? Do all benchmarks have these dimensions? If not, can we omit ones that have 0,0 for them to avoid clutter?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 670,
        "startChar": 59,
        "endLine": 670,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "47af5aed5a7a3a6b305820d692b79f0336dc0d60",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "29584768_b3e7311d",
        "filename": "bench/BazelBenchmarkRunner.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 670,
      "author": {
        "id": 10009
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-10-05T19:45:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "You\u0027re right, it makes more sense to make a trace ID unique by expressing the width, height, scale, etc. as their own keys rather than by generating a unique test name from them.\n\nAlso, having both a \"name\" and a \"test\" key is confusing.\n\nDropping \"test\" and adding keys \"width\" and \"height\".\n\nI left a note to also add \"scale\" and whatever else is necessary when we add support for `SKPBench` and `SKPAnimationBench`.\n\nThere is some value in keeping `Benchmark::getUniqueName()` around in that it can disambiguate log messages. But that\u0027s a separate issue which we can discuss and tackle independently.",
      "parentUuid": "34f04a54_e5705325",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 670,
        "startChar": 59,
        "endLine": 670,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "47af5aed5a7a3a6b305820d692b79f0336dc0d60",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
